  "narrative": "No independent validation result or validation-response deadline is currently listed, so synthesis focuses on the discovery evidence now in the ledger. I accept H13: in this supplied dataset, feature_010 = 1 versus 0 has a signed positive mean difference of +0.829 composite dependency-score units (95% Welch interval approximately +0.767 to +0.891). This is far above the +0.15 threshold and is not sensitive to the 12-comparison discovery screening burden. Because lower outcome_001 values indicate stronger dependency, the positive raw contrast corresponds to weaker composite dependency in the feature_010 = 1 group relative to the comparator. This claim is limited to an association in the supplied observational dataset. Its unusually large magnitude, together with the opaque predictor construction, warrants caution about confounding, measurement overlap, or leakage; it is not evidence of causality or external generalizability.\n\nThe original H5 remains rejected because its registered negative direction was strongly contradicted by the same underlying contrast. H1-H4, H6-H8, H11, and H12 remain rejected: neither main associations nor interactions provided evidence exceeding the threshold in their claimed directions. H9 remains unresolved and deferred because its interaction point estimate is small (+0.048) and only its upper interval narrowly crosses +0.15, while the corresponding marker main effect is null. H10 remains unresolved and active because it is the strongest tested interaction signal (point +0.091, upper interval +0.206), though the current evidence does not establish a threshold-exceeding interaction.\n\nThe most informative next step is to analyze the already registered feature_010 follow-up claims H14-H21. These will determine whether the large feature_010 association is approximately uniform or concentrated by feature_038, feature_018, feature_036, or feature_058, and will provide within-stratum information for H10. If an independent validation result becomes available or is requested after these subgroup analyses, the highest-priority validation target is H13, with a subgroup-supported refinement considered only if the new evidence justifies a narrower claim.",
  "research_notes": "Phase 1 synthesis update:\n- Accepted: H13. feature_010=1 vs 0 positive mean difference +0.829 (CI +0.767 to +0.891), dataset-only observational association. Keep active to characterize heterogeneity, not because causal interpretation is established.\n- Rejected/closed: H1-H4, H6-H8, H11-H12; original H5 direction is wrong and rejected.\n- Deferred/unresolved: H9 feature_007-by-feature_036; point estimate too small and marker main effect null.\n- Active/unresolved: H10 feature_058-by-feature_038; strongest interaction signal but not threshold-supported.\n- Pending next analyses: H14-H21. Priority is localizing feature_010 and evaluating feature_038/feature_058 modification.\n- Validation plan: after H14-H21 results, use the next appraise opportunity to request validation for H13 if still scientifically warranted. Treat leakage/confounding concerns explicitly because effect is very large."
}
